  "subdivision_of_building": "Existing ground floor accessible toilet & adjoined garages, garage forecourt and entry ramp, standalone garages, and boundary fence. ",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "The facility at Louise House, Brookscroft Road provides a day centre offering special facilities for adults with a disability. The day centre has been operated by Vibrance (formerly RCHL) since 2010 and acts as a base for local service users in the Waltham Forest area. \n\nThe proposal provides much needed additional accessible toilets and changing facilities, improved parking and manoeuvrability for minibuses used by the service, remediation and improvement of water damaged areas of the facade, reconfiguration the accessible entrance ramp, and modernisation of the existing perimeter fence and entry gate. The proposal does not plan to change the massing of the site, aside from the demolition of existing standalone garages, separated from the main building by a vehicular garage court. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and thereafter maintained as such for the lifetime of the development: - drawing number (add reference number)dated (date on the plans)",
    "&lt;p&gt;All designated accessible bays should be marked up as disabled persons parking bays from \r\nthe outset and should remain clearly marked for the lifetime of the development.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Within 1 month of completion, a photographic survey &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;of the adjoining carriageway and footway on\r\nBrookscroft and Woodend Roads pre-commencement and post-completion shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval. The condition survey should cover the site\r\nfrontage and 20m on both sides including any area on the public highway identified. The condition survey must include a site plan showing\r\nthe location of where the photographs were taken on the public highway.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
